  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Publish after a re-translation now puts the newly imported translation live. On a second translation cycle Publish resolved the published version and republished a clone of it, leaving the translation just imported as an untouched draft: live content silently reverted to the first translation while the job still reported Published, with no error. Publish now resolves the common draft — the same version Optimizely's own Publish Changes button acts on — and falls back to the published version when no draft resolves, so first-cycle and no-pending-edit publishes are unaffected.",
